  "worked_solution": "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ k & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-6+3)+(-3k+1)+2(3k-2) \\\\  & =-18-3k+1+6k-4 \\\\  & =3k-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{3k-21}{-9}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9}{3k-21} & =1 \\\\ -9 & =3k-21 \\\\ 12 & =3k \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
